 30 PRINT
OK
HELP SAVE
SAVE "name"
  Writes the program to the file as LIST shows it, with no space before a
  line number. A file of that name is replaced. Ends a program.
  SAVE "HELLO.BAS"

OK
NEW

OK
10 OPEN 1,"T.BAS":OPEN 2,"HELLO.BAS"
20 FOR L=1 TO 2:A$="":B$=""
30 GET#1,C$:GET#2,D$:IF C$<>CHR$(13) THEN A$=A$+C$:B$=B$+D$:GOTO 30
40 PRINT A$:PRINT B$:NEXT:CLOSE 1:CLOSE 2
RUN
10 PRINT "SAVED"
10 PRINT "HELLO 
20 FOR I=1 TO 2:PRINT I;:NEXT
ROM A FILE"
20 FOR I=1 TO 3:P

OK
NEW

OK
10 PRINT "NEW TEXT"
SAVE "T.BAS"

OK
NAME "T.BAS" AS "U.BAS"

OK
NAME "U.BAS" AS "HELLO.BAS"

?FILE EXISTS ERROR
OK
NAME "NOSUCH.BAS" AS "V.BAS"

?FILE NOT FOUND ERROR
OK
LOAD "T.BAS"

?FILE NOT FOUND ERROR
OK
LOAD "U.BAS"

OK
LIST

 10 PRINT "NEW TEXT"
OK
KILL "U.BAS"

OK
KILL "U.BAS"

?FILE NOT FOUND ERROR
OK
HELP NAME
NAME "old" AS "new"
  Renames a file or a directory, or moves a file to another directory of the
  same drive. A new name that exists gives ?FILE EXISTS ERROR.
  NAME "OLD.BAS" AS "NEW.BAS"

OK
HELP KILL
KILL "name"
  Deletes the file. Close it first.
  KILL "OLD.BAS"

OK
QUIT
C>TYPE HELLO.BAS
10 PRINT "HELLO FROM A FILE"
20 FOR I=1 TO 3:PRINT I;:NEXT
30 PRINT
